Update the 3D landscape artist portfolio website with the following specific requirements.

## Artist Information

Artist name: Abid Hossain

Profession: 3D Landscape Artist

Create a sophisticated, minimalist, premium portfolio that showcases his 3D landscape artwork. The website should feel like a high-end digital art gallery with elegant typography, beautiful imagery, generous whitespace, and subtle animations.

## 1. Multilingual Support — English, Bangla, Japanese

The website must support three languages:

- English (EN)
- বাংলা (BN)
- 日本語 (JA)

**Default language: English.**

Add a clean, elegant language switcher in the top navigation, preferably a compact dropdown or segmented selector.

Requirements:
- English must be selected on the first visit by default.
- Users can switch between English, Bangla, and Japanese.
- All interface text must change when the language changes, including navigation, headings, descriptions, buttons, category labels, contact section, footer, and artwork-related UI.
- Implement actual translations, not just language labels.
- Use natural, professional translations for all three languages.
- Keep the selected language while navigating between the homepage and admin dashboard.
- Use a simple, maintainable translation dictionary with separate English, Bangla, and Japanese translation objects.
- Avoid translating the artist's name, artwork titles, and original artwork descriptions automatically. Preserve original content unless a translated version is explicitly provided.
- For Japanese, use an appropriate Japanese font fallback.
- Ensure Bangla text renders correctly using a suitable Bengali font, such as Noto Sans Bengali.
- Use locale-aware typography and spacing without breaking the design.

The language switcher should look like a natural part of the website, not a large or distracting control.

## 2. Artist Profile and Photo

Display the artist's name as:

Abid Hossain

Use the professional title:

3D Landscape Artist

I have provided the artist's photograph as an uploaded reference image. Use that provided photograph for the artist portrait if it is available to the project. Do not replace it with a random person or generate a different identity.

Place a small, elegant artist portrait in the About section or near the hero introduction. Keep the landscape artwork as the primary visual focus.

If the provided portrait is not accessible during generation, use a clearly replaceable placeholder and make the portrait image source configurable from the artist profile data.

Do not invent personal biography, achievements, awards, qualifications, or work history. Use editable placeholder text until I add the actual information.

## 3. Public Portfolio — One Page

Keep the public portfolio as a single, scrollable homepage at `/`.

Include these sections:

1. Minimal navigation with artist name, Selected Works, About, Contact, and language switcher.
2. Hero section with a cinematic 3D landscape artwork and the headline "Imagining Landscapes Beyond Reality."
3. Selected Works gallery with category filters.
4. About the Artist section with Abid Hossain's portrait and editable biography.
5. Creative Approach section.
6. Contact section with email, phone, and WhatsApp actions.
7. Minimal footer.

Use a warm off-white background, charcoal typography, muted olive accents, and elegant editorial serif headings.

Make the website visually impressive, responsive, and polished on desktop and mobile.

## 4. Artwork Gallery and Empty State

I will add the actual artwork images and descriptions later through the admin dashboard.

Therefore, create a gallery that works with an initially empty artwork dataset.

When there are no uploaded artworks, display an elegant empty state, such as:

"New landscapes are coming soon."

Translate this message into Bangla and Japanese.

Do not permanently hardcode sample artworks into the public gallery. If sample data is used during development, clearly separate it from real artwork data and make it easy to remove.

Each real artwork should support:
- Image
- Artwork title
- Category
- Original description
- Optional year
- Optional featured status
- Optional translations of the title and description for Bangla and Japanese

Show only actual published artworks on the public website.

The category filters must be generated from available artwork categories. Selecting a category should filter the gallery correctly.

Clicking an artwork should open an elegant lightbox with the full image, title, description, category, and previous/next navigation where practical.

## 5. Admin Dashboard — /admin

Create a separate admin dashboard at `/admin`.

This dashboard is intended for me to manage the portfolio in the future. I need to be able to add artwork images and descriptions myself.

Create a practical artwork management interface with:

### Add Artwork
- Upload an image using a file input.
- Preview the selected image before saving.
- Enter artwork title.
- Select or create a category.
- Write an artwork description.
- Optionally enter the year.
- Mark an artwork as featured.
- Add optional Bangla and Japanese translations of the title and description.
- Set publication status to Draft or Published.

### Manage Artwork
- View uploaded artwork records.
- Edit existing artwork details.
- Replace artwork images.
- Delete artwork after confirmation.
- Publish or unpublish artwork.
- Preview the artwork before publishing.
- Search and filter artwork by title, category, and status.

### Manage Artist Profile
Provide editable fields for:
- Artist name: Abid Hossain
- Artist portrait
- Biography in English
- Biography in Bangla
- Biography in Japanese
- Email address
- Phone number
- WhatsApp number

### Admin Experience

Keep the admin interface clean, professional, and easy to use.

Provide form validation, helpful error messages, upload previews, confirmation dialogs, and clear save/cancel actions.

Separate the admin interface from the public navigation.

Do not expose administrative editing controls on the public homepage.

## 6. Backend-Ready Architecture

I will implement the backend myself later.

For now:
- Build the entire frontend using Next.js App Router, React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS.
- Use reusable components and centralized data models.
- Create a clean data-access layer or repository abstraction for artwork and artist profile data.
- Use mock data or local state only where necessary for the prototype.
- Make the frontend easy to connect to my future API.
- Clearly distinguish temporary local previews from permanently stored images.
- Do not claim that uploaded images or edited records are permanently saved unless persistent storage actually exists.
- Keep the data model ready for database records and image-storage URLs.
- Include fields for original text and optional English, Bangla, and Japanese translations.

Important: browser local state alone is not permanent storage. If you choose localStorage for a frontend-only prototype, explain its limitations and keep the storage logic isolated so it can be replaced with API calls later.

Do not add a database or external storage service at this stage.

## 7. Contact Actions

Provide configurable contact details in the artist profile.

Include:
- Email Me
- Call Me
- WhatsApp

Use correct `mailto:`, `tel:`, and `https://wa.me/` links.

Do not invent real email addresses or phone numbers. If contact details have not been entered, hide or disable the corresponding action rather than showing a fake contact link.

Translate button labels into all three supported languages.

## 8. Technical and Design Requirements

- Next.js App Router
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui where appropriate
- Lucide icons
- Responsive desktop, tablet, and mobile layouts
- Accessible controls and keyboard navigation
- Reduced-motion support
- Correct image aspect ratios
- Optimized image rendering
- Functional language switching
- Functional gallery filters and lightbox
- Functional frontend admin forms and CRUD interactions

Keep the public homepage as a single page and the admin dashboard at `/admin`.

Do not create unnecessary extra public pages.

## Final Goal

Build a refined multilingual portfolio for Abid Hossain that feels like a bespoke digital art gallery.

English must be the default language, with Bangla and Japanese available through the language switcher.

Use the provided artist photograph if accessible. Allow me to add actual artwork images, titles, categories, descriptions, and translations later through the admin dashboard.

Prioritize elegant visual design, simplicity, accurate multilingual behavior, and an architecture that will make future backend integration straightforward.

Build the complete working frontend rather than just a static wireframe.